      "writtenOn": "2024-08-26T08:22:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The setSecure sets the last value (i.e. before the fix, the isSecure wasn\u0027t used at all).\nBefore - for an http request, the value is always set to the authConfig.getCookieSecure (last setSecure call). If authConfig.getCookieSecure is true, the auth cookie is not stored/accepted by a client at all (https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies#block_access_to_your_cookies - \"Insecure sites (with http: in the URL) can\u0027t set cookies with the Secure attribute\").\nIn other words, if owner wants secure cookies and the owner sets auth.cookiesecure to true, then (even if the server is accessible by http) the cookies are safe.\n\nAfter - now if auth.cookiesecure is true and client makes http request - the \"secure\" flag is not set for cookies. So a) they will be stored on the client b) they will not be marked as secure and will be transferred back to server with http requests too (not only with https).\n\nAm I missed something? Maybe just keep the last line:\n  outCookie.setSecure(authConfig.getCookieSecure());\n?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "4b9dac71b71d8d01344afe665f226f74d1a18a42",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5223421_8c195d64",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/httpd/CacheBasedWebSession.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065256
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-26T08:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I missed that.\nMy thoughts were rather along the line: If you enable the use of HTTP but use secure Cookies, it doesn\u0027t make sense. If you perform an HTTP request, sending the cookie via HTTPS doesn\u0027t make sense and as I now know, wouldn\u0027t even work. But if it doesn\u0027t work, in that case the UI would be unusable, since users wouldn\u0027t be able to have a cookie-based web session in that scenario.\n\nWhile I believe that this change should then be reverted, I believe:\n\n- we should adapt the same behaviour for the XsrfCookie, which I used as a template for what I did in this change.\n- we should consider whether we should not simplify the configuration over all, e.g. if HTTPS is being used (https or proxy-https in listenAddress), use secure cookies, instead of using separate configuration options, which just complicate things and lead to insecure configurations, because users just miss it.",
      "parentUuid": "2629b754_4ed436fc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "4b9dac71b71d8d01344afe665f226f74d1a18a42",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45412531_5940353d",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/httpd/CacheBasedWebSession.java",
